  "translationRepairs": [
    ["s0028","literal","When histories of several generations are thus, their deeds grow dim: even rulers who rode with the times to win fame and ministers who plotted together have none who could plainly stir the eyes and ears of the world and claim the mouths of the world.","When histories of several generations are thus, their deeds grow dim: even among rulers who rode with the times to win fame and ministers who plotted together, none could plainly stir the eyes and ears of the world and claim the mouths of the world.","Chinese 雖有…之君…之臣，未有…者也 means that although such rulers and ministers existed, none of them achieved renown that stirred the world's eyes and ears; the original 'have none who could' misconstrues that construction, and the proposed 'even among…, none could…' restores the sense accurately.","high","applied"]
  ],
